  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Every item is closed except two. The pt-0007 chest X-ray is preliminary only, so it is left open on purpose (§2c). The pt-0065 fax is reassigned to RN triage because I could not confirm which patient it belongs to.\n\n**Closed with no action needed**\n- **pt-0016:** TSH 2.1, normal. The potassium 6.3 was corrected by the lab to 4.4 (analyzer calibration fault), so I acted on 4.4: normal.\n- **pt-0007 CTA chest (preliminary):** the final report (dr-00084) shows no PE and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a vessel). Closed: no follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\n- **pt-0064:** creatinine 1.36 (9/26) and the new 1.48 (10/22). Neither has an earlier creatinine within 48 h or 7 days, so neither meets the kidney-injury rule.\n- **pt-0033, creatinine 1.31:** the 10/21 value is marked entered in error and was not used. The lowest valid value in the prior 7 days is 1.27, so this result does not meet the rule.\n\n**Closed with action**\n- **pt-0007, BMP 10/22 – acute kidney injury:** creatinine 1.64, up from 0.98 about 35 h earlier. Urgent repeat BMP ordered for by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0009), patient messaged and told to avoid NSAIDs, note written. Naproxen PRN is still active and left unchanged for your review.\n- **pt-0033, new creatinine 1.78 (St. Brigid urgent care) – acute kidney injury:** up 0.47 from 1.31 nine hours earlier. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0025), patient messaged, note written.\n- **pt-0008, potassium 6.4:**\n  - It was first flagged hemolyzed, so I followed the hemolyzed pathway: urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0016) and a patient message.\n  - A correction then arrived: the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient's specimen, so 6.4 stands.\n  - I switched to the stat pathway: stat BMP today (sr-t0020), on-call notified at stat priority, a corrected message telling the patient to come in today, and an addendum note.\n  - Medication review found nothing that raises potassium; nothing held.\n  - sr-t0016 is superseded, but I could not withdraw it with the tools I have.\n- **pt-0006 (Raj Patel), lung nodule:**\n  - At first I treated the 4 mm LLL nodule on his CT urogram as incidental in a high-risk smoker. I ordered a CT chest for Sep–Nov 2027 (sr-t0001) with a tracking task, and messaged him.\n  - Then a Lakeshore addendum arrived: a new 5 mm RUL nodule on his 4/14 screening scan, Lung-RADS 3, repeat low-dose CT in 6 months. This showed he is already in lung cancer screening, and the LLL nodule is the one they follow. A screening report from 4/14 was already in his chart and I missed it on the first pass.\n  - Corrected plan: screening low-dose CT ordered for 10/23–11/14 (sr-t0030) with a tracking task due 11/14, a corrected patient message, and an addendum note.\n  - I could not withdraw sr-t0001 or its tracking task (task-t0002). **You need to discontinue them** — task-t0032 (due 10/26) asks you to, and says not to schedule sr-t0001.\n\n**Still open**\n- **pt-0065 Lakeshore fax (Lung-RADS 4A):** the fax gives DOB 1951-08-04 and MRN 4471-20. Our Judith Nowicki is DOB 1960-03-22, MRN 0388-83, and no patient matches the fax. Nothing was written to her chart. Reassigned to RN triage to contact Lakeshore, get the result to the right patient's clinician, and have the fax removed from her chart.\n- **pt-0007 chest X-ray (dr-06204):** preliminary read shows a possible 7 mm RUL opacity. No final report yet, so the item stays open and no action was taken.\n\nYour seven messages-queue items (refill requests) were not touched.",
